  "statuteText": "227-C:24 Review Process Established; Purpose. –\n\nThere is hereby established a review process, which shall be administered by the director of the division of historical resources, to insure the protection of designated New Hampshire heritage landmarks. The purpose of the review process is to protect the environmental integrity of designated historic landmarks from events which would diminish their heritage value for future generations as educational and inspirational assets of the state."
